  {
    "sha": "ecb54b7f339dcc8c7031a32d7eda9e76f3019af2",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKGVjYjU0YjdmMzM5ZGNjOGM3MDMxYTMyZDdlZGE5ZTc2ZjMwMTlhZjI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-11T18:26:42Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-11T18:26:42Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(adaptive): refuse on heavy geometry only over a long walk; keep the STEP bore's plan\n\nThe vertex-only budget cut a level of the user's STEP bore (app\npocket3d_hsm heavy lane) that plans on main: 33 revolutions over a\nfinely tessellated outline, 1.14 M vertices but only 2.6 k r of walk.\nMeasured, the planner's time grows with the square of the ring's vertex\ncount, and the bore is the slowest plan of all (200 s of growth), so no\ntime-faithful unit keeps it and refuses the island sooner. The rule now\nrefuses a plan past 600 k vertices AND 5,000 tool radii of revolutions:\nevery plan that finishes on main is light (<= 358 k) or short (the\nbore); the island, the stepped block and the rotary developed levels -\nrefused on main by length - are refused sooner, by name.\n\nThe bore test now pins its per-level strategy (only Z 20's crossing\nplan goes to the rings) and prints a path digest, identical to main's.\n\nFixes #850\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
