      "message": "test(adaptive): island pin to the heavy lane with a fast twin; plain refusal text; NaN length pinned\n\nReview round on PR #865:\n- the full island pin (46-59 s debug) moves to the heavy lane; a fast\n  default-suite twin drives the planner's own loop at lowered law-3\n  limits through a test-only Work::with_limits passed to plan_within\n  (1.9 s debug) and pins the named refusal with no passes;\n- the geometry refusal says plainly that both limits were passed\n  (outline too detailed and path too long, each with its limit);\n- a NaN/non-positive revolution length neither refuses nor switches\n  law 2 off (a deliberate change for degenerate input), pinned;\n- the bore test asserts its path counts (5530 moves, 5497 planar,\n  600 arcs) instead of printing an unstable digest;\n- push_walk moves from mod.rs to grow.rs so mod.rs does not grow.\n\nRefs #850\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
